  "body": "On iOS a control cannot show its picker without having focus. Should the web developer handle that or should `showPicker()` handle it for them? The latter seems somewhat reasonable given the current description of `showPicker()` (in particular the last step of \"show the picker, if applicable\"), but this would be worth calling out explicitly given the additional events that would end up firing.\r\n\r\nThoughts?",
